# The claat binary every path uses, in one place.
#
# Sourced by website/deploy.sh, website/tool/export_codelabs.sh and both
# website workflows. Before this file existed, the workflows pinned
# claat-linux-amd64 by SHA-256 while deploy.sh took whatever `claat` was on
# PATH — so the two paths that can publish the live site disagreed on the
# binary whose output every guard in export_codelabs.sh is calibrated against.
# On the maintainer's machine that was 2.2.5 against CI's 2.2.6.
#
# The release tag is mutable, which is why the bytes are pinned rather than the
# tag. There is no darwin-arm64 build; Apple Silicon runs the amd64 one under
# Rosetta.
#
# To bump: change CLAAT_VERSION, download each asset, record its sha256 here,
# then run tool/export_codelabs.sh and confirm the page checks still pass —
# a claat that emits a different resource URL will fail the allowlist, which is
# exactly what it is there for.

CLAAT_VERSION=v2.2.6
CLAAT_BASE_URL=https://github.com/googlecodelabs/tools/releases/download

CLAAT_SHA256_darwin_amd64=3ba3eebec664076123626c2c77674f7779d5fc5647c53d180399183a3ba31695
CLAAT_SHA256_linux_amd64=b7415471bd823562ebd9e6015e267a12fbf9340dfe839f8e2a175b6c7c0f397a
